/ item-doors: a type is born whole (the type that makes a value hands itself to it), one door for
/ writing, a type speaks for itself to a writer, a type's members through its own list, and a plang
/ value read as tokens. This goal is the plan's index and its proof: each stage is a goal, each
/ comment a behaviour we want, and the step under it runs the test that proves it. Tests live under
/ this plan's folder at the path of what they test. The plang here is intent: the test-designer
/ writes each test so it builds and goes red before its stage, the coder makes it green. The text
/ is start.md; checks tests can't show are there too.
Start
- call Stage1
- call Stage2
- call Stage3
- call Stage4
- call Stage5

Stage1
/ a type is born whole (decision 867): the registered type hands itself to the value
/ an image value's kind knows its mime: a {image, kind: png} carries image/png from the registered kind, not an inline copy
- call /plan/item-doors/app/type/image/BytesKnowItsMime
/ a type named in a step is the registered one: its kind knows its mime and its extension
- call /plan/item-doors/app/type/text/NamedTypeIsRegistered
/ text's face without the name floor: the kind carries IsText; a {text, kind: md} answers true itself, not through the Name fallback
- call /plan/item-doors/app/type/text/TextKindIsText
/ "is this an action slot?" by type, not by name — C# test at PLang.Tests/Runtime/App/Goals/ActionSlotIsByTypeTests.cs
/ (a fresh type.@this("action") has no ClrType; the registered one does — today the Name compare can't tell them apart)
/ an image made from bytes holds its registered kind — C# test at PLang.Tests/Types/App/Types/ImageKindKnowsItsMimeTests.cs
/ (today image/this.cs:189 makes its kind from a name, so Type.kind.Mime is empty — the registered image.kind.png's image/png never reaches it)
/ a plain text's own kind answers it's characters — C# test at PLang.Tests/Types/App/Types/TextKindIsTextByItselfTests.cs
/ (today text's own format has no Text=true, so Type.kind.IsText is false and source.cs:115 patches it with _type.Name is "text")
/ the four kind/strict tests are this stage's proof: adopted from test/app/type/kind/strict/
- call /app/type/kind/strict/SetAsImageGifStrictMatching
- call /app/type/kind/strict/SetAsImageGifStrictMismatch
- call /app/type/kind/strict/SetAsImageStrictNoKind
- call /app/type/kind/strict/SetAsTextSlashMarkdownStrictUnverifiable
/ a plural plang reaches is a singular node (item-doors 39): a dict's key read alone is its first key, .list every key
- call /plan/item-doors/app/type/dict/key/KeyIsTheFirstKey
/ a click's modifier read alone is the first key held, .list every one (item-doors 41)
- call /plan/item-doors/app/type/input/modifier/ModifierIsTheFirstKeyHeld

Stage2
/ one door for writing (decision 868): Output only; the sync Write and the IsLeaf branch go;
/ the writer carries its output kind (an object, not a string); Owns and its 5 checks go;
/ the byte door Bytes(byte[], kind) replaces Bytes(byte[]) and Raw(byte[]) (844);
/ a pair registry (846) looks up how an input kind looks in an output kind, in one place (data.Output)

Stage3
/ a type speaks for itself to a writer (decision 869): Data always calls BeginRecord/EndRecord,
/ each writer decides what to show; bare json shows only the value; plang's own writer is its own
/ output kind with {type, value, signature} on the wire, name only in Store; the llm table learns
/ a column's type from the record (815); EmitsSchema and Data's two ifs on it go (813); the first
/ pair-registry entries are each type's JSON Schema for llm-provider's tools

Stage4
/ reading a plang value as tokens (decision 871): a structural IReader over a value in hand
/ (type/format/item/reader.cs, NEW): a dict as an object, a list as an array, a leaf as its token;
/ Step.Set reads every row one way, FromJson and the is-dict-or-list branches go;
/ item.Set's C# lowering fallback goes

Stage5
/ a type's members through its own list (decision 870, 872): item.Get/Set go through type.Property
/ (property.Read/Write, NEW); IsDefault compares the value with the default made as the property's
/ type; reflection only where property is built; a key the type has no member for is ADDED
/ (not refused), the only refusal is writing over an own member that can't be written
